[31m-5. What Is a Domain Name?[m
[31m-A domain name is the website's easy-to-remember address. It is what people type into a browser to visit the business online.[m
[31m-Simple example[m
[31m-A domain could look like gagisacco.co.ke. It is similar to the physical address of a business, but it is the address of the business online.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-A domain normally has to be registered and renewed. The price depends on the type of domain and the company used to register it.[m
[31m-.co.ke  --  commonly associated with Kenyan businesses.[m
[31m-.com  --  widely recognised internationally.[m
[31m-.ke  --  a shorter Kenyan domain option.[m
[31m-6. What Is Hosting?[m
[31m-Hosting is the service that stores the website's files and makes them available on the internet. Think of it as renting space where the website lives.[m
[31m-Simple comparison[m
[31m-Domain = the address people use to find the website.[m
[31m-Hosting = the place where the website lives.[m
[31m-Website files = the actual building, rooms, signs and information inside that place.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Hosting is normally paid for periodically, often yearly. The cost depends on the hosting company, type of hosting and resources required.[m
